@crew quist-ilse
// Ilse Quist (they/them), Works technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Slow, dry; herbs as friends.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh, hello. You're new. The garden's on Deck 3, if you need to stand somewhere green.
- Hm? Hi. If a job says garden pumps, bring a towel. Trust me.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Oh, hello. The basil grew overnight. It's very pleased with itself.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hello, you. Have you watered anything today? Not you. A plant.
? tier>=colleague
- {me}. I'm on chapter three and I know who did it. I'm going to keep reading anyway.
? tier>=friend
- Oh, it's you. Good. The thyme likes you. It said so. It didn't. It would.   #warm

== bye
- Bye, then. Mind the basil.
- See you. I'll be with the herbs. They're better listeners than most.   #funny

== feel
? mood:low
- The parsley's wilting. I'm taking it personally.
? mood:high
- Brennan used my herbs tonight. She said so. Out loud. In front of people.

== near
? act:work
- Pump's fine. I just like it down here. It smells of the garden.
? act:leisure
- Same mystery, chapter nine. I was right in chapter three. Still reading.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I grow herbs on the bunk windowsill for the galley. The basil's a bit of a show-off.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- Moreau guesses by chapter two. I guess by chapter three. We're both wrong half the time.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Rub a basil leaf. Go on. Smell your fingers. That's the whole summer, right there.
